; GraphEdit whose minimap draws a connection polyline at the DEFAULT
; antialiasing. `GraphEditMinimap` redraws every connection inside its own
; panel with `draw_polyline_colors(points, colors, 0.5, lines_antialiased)`
; (graph_edit.cpp:1611) — the only reader of `connection_lines_antialiased`
; anywhere in the engine (graph_edit.h:254, default true). At width 0.5 the
; antialiased branch adds a feather of FEATHER_SIZE * width = 0.625px on each
; side plus a cap at each end (renderer_canvas_cull.cpp:1030-1163), which is
; most of the line's drawn area at that width.
; unit-graph-edit.tscn is the only other scene carrying a `connections` entry
; and it sets `connection_lines_antialiased = false`, so the feathered branch
; is drawn in no other fixture — and a previewer that ignored the property
; would score identically on both files while drawing one of them wrong.
; Two GraphNodes, one right port and one left port, are the minimum a
; resolvable connection needs; the rest of the file is this family's shared
; GraphEdit rect.

; Every fixture in this family shares one GraphEdit rect and one GraphNode,
; and `scroll_offset` is deliberately ABSENT from all but
; unit-graph-edit-scroll-offset-clamped.tscn, which exists to move it:
; GraphEdit's own `set_scroll_offset` clamps against min/max bounds no laid-out
; child has widened while a scene's properties are applied (graph_edit.cpp:407),
; so an authored offset moves the grid, the nodes AND the minimap camera at once
; and would mask the one variable each file exists to move.
